<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 21 September, from 454 to 1981.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">International Day of Peace</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">Established by the United Nations in 1981 and observed with a global ceasefire since 2001, the International Day of Peace invites all nations and peoples to commit to peace above all differences and to contribute to building a culture of peace.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">454 <span class="tih-ago">1,572 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Valentinian III murders his general Aetius</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Valentinian III killed Flavius Aetius with his own hands during a meeting in Ravenna. The West lost the commander who had checked Attila; Valentinian was himself assassinated six months later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1327 <span class="tih-ago">699 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Deposed Edward II dies at Berkeley Castle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Edward II was announced dead at Berkeley Castle, almost certainly murdered on the orders of Queen Isabella and Roger Mortimer. The later tale of a red-hot poker is unsupported.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1745 <span class="tih-ago">281 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jacobites rout a government army at Prestonpans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bonnie Prince Charlie's Highlanders routed Sir John Cope's army in a few minutes near Edinburgh. The victory encouraged the Jacobite invasion of England, which turned back at Derby.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1866 <span class="tih-ago">160 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">H. G. Wells is born in Bromley</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Herbert George Wells was born in Kent to a shopkeeper's family. His novels The Time Machine and The War of the Worlds helped found modern science fiction.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guatemala.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1981 <span class="tih-ago">45 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Belize becomes independent</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The former British Honduras became independent as Belize, with George Price as prime minister. British troops remained because Guatemala claimed the territory; it recognised Belize in 1991.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a></div></div></li></ol>
